  "implemented": [
    "A bounded distinct CONTROL container drains only already-ready progress updates without collection sleeps or DATA borrowing. Three simultaneous credit updates execute as one actual accounted mail in the new integration regression.",
    "A lone control keeps its original packet geometry, so an original exact-size one-message grant is not stranded by optional container overhead. Existing payload/response/crypto/account/grant/session bounds remain authoritative.",
    "OPEN and RESET remain single publications; they cannot couple allocating/tombstone work to progress-only inbox admission. Whole-container generation, ledger, AEAD and semantic validation precede replay commit.",
    "Exact prepared-body outcome/proof handling applies atomically to all live members. Physical acceptance does not become peer receipt or quota refund. Workers use the same actual selected sockets and CONTROL authority."
  ],
  "retained_failures": [
    "The initial current-container cohort exceeds the unchanged 64-message fast-mailbox cap in the fluctuating command-service cold case.",
    "The final whole-core cohort exceeds the same unchanged bound in the no-delay cold case. These cases remain failures; no scenario, first run, mailbox/grant limit, deadline, fsync requirement or performance threshold was changed to obtain a pass."
  ],
  "validation": [
    "18/18 targeted top-level group executions pass with race detection, covering three new container/grant/authentication tests and three existing inbox-pressure/debt regressions.",
    "The final whole-core source cohort passes 175 of 176 top-level groups. The one cold failure is retained with raw flow, command, journal and runtime evidence.",
    "10 native top-level groups pass with race detection; core vet passes.",
    "This demonstrates less physical control-mail amplification for simultaneously ready updates. It does not demonstrate elimination of cold failures, sustained bandwidth, RTT improvement, or improvement over field RC2."
  ],
  "remaining_for_first_rc": [
    "Production long-lived rendezvous/selector and agreed roster/READY integration from the real profile, with actual permanent-keyword capability verification and original socket budgets.",
    "DATA/CONTROL offer turnover, usage/retirement/proof reclamation and full in-place legacy journal/wallet recovery. Standing rendezvous, key establishment and finite initial permissions alone do not supply a sustained datapath.",
    "Receiver-window/controller integration, native/TUN/Android API activation, and unchanged application/performance/stability qualification. StartClient and ServeManaged still fail closed; an APK compiled around them would not carry traffic."
  ],
  "artifacts": "No APK, deployable server binary or release tag. Source checkpoints are pushed to the existing development branch; signing identity and DNS behavior are unchanged."
}
